# Desktop entries hidden from every launcher (quickshell's AppMenu, rofi, KDE).
# One desktop-file id per line, no .desktop suffix; blank lines and # comments
# are ignored. link.sh writes a NoDisplay override into
# ~/.local/share/applications for each, which is the XDG-sanctioned way to hide
# a package's entry without deleting a file pacman owns.
#
# plasma-bigscreen is a TV shell pulled in by the `plasma` group. Its launcher
# entry runs plasma-bigscreen-swap-session, which only works from inside a KDE
# session — from this Hyprland desktop it exits immediately and the launcher
# reports "failed to launch process 127". The other entries below are its
# settings modules, which are KCMs for that same TV shell.
plasma-bigscreen-swap-session
org.kde.plasma.bigscreen.inputhandler
org.kde.plasma.bigscreen.uvcviewer
kcm_mediacenter_audiodevice
kcm_mediacenter_bigscreen_settings
kcm_mediacenter_bluetooth
kcm_mediacenter_display
kcm_mediacenter_input
kcm_mediacenter_kdeconnect
kcm_mediacenter_wallpaper
kcm_mediacenter_webapps
kcm_mediacenter_wifi
